Article 14
(1) The handling of child victims of violence as referred to in Article 11 letter b shall be implemented in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.
(2) In handling child victims of violence as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government may cooperate with:
a. vertical agencies;
b. provincial government;
c. other regency/city governments;
d. village government;
e. non-governmental organizations;
f. private parties;
g. the community; and/or
h. families.

Article 9
(1) The Forms of Protection Services for Women Victims of Violence as referred to in Article 8 include:
a. legal aid services;
b. health services;
c. social rehabilitation services;
d. repatriation and social reintegration services;
e. complaint, consultation, and counseling services; and/or
f. assistance services.
(2) In addition to the Protection Services for Women Victims of Violence as referred to in paragraph (1), Services are carried out by receiving and sending case referrals from and/or to other service units in a networked manner.
(3) The implementation of Protection Services for Women Victims of Violence as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be carried out by the Regional Apparatus responsible for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection.
(4) Further provisions regarding the forms and procedures of Protection Services for Women Victims of Violence as referred to in paragraph (1) through paragraph (3) shall be regulated by a Mayor Regulation.

Article 24
The duties and functions of FPKK as referred to in Article 23 consist of:
a. coordinating and synchronizing prevention, services, and empowerment for women and children victims of violence;
b. maintaining and developing FPKK in prevention, services, and empowerment of victims through networking and referral systems;
c. conducting education on non-discrimination values towards women and children;
d. conducting socialization of laws and regulations related to the implementation of Protection for Women and Children Victims of Violence;
e. collecting, compiling, and presenting data reports on victims of violence; and
f. conducting monitoring and evaluation of the implementation of Protection for Women and Children Victims of Violence.

